 "_model_notes": [
  "NaCl crystallization by evaporation followed by cooling and ideal solid/liquid separation. The 26 wt% feed is undersaturated at room temperature; a filter cannot extract dissolved salt.",
  "EV-101 concentrates feed to 28 wt% NaCl; outlet 111.85 C and 1.013 bar are declared operating conditions approximating atmospheric brine boiling with boiling-point elevation. The model does not predict electrolyte vapor-liquid equilibrium.",
  "R-101 represents cooling crystallizer plus ideal solids recovery, with pure dry crystals and saturated mother liquor at 295 K. Yield = 1 means all available supersaturation; it does not mean all salt crystallizes.",
  "Specified solubility = 6.142 mol NaCl/kg water times 58.44 g/mol at 295 K, IUPAC 2022 Table 7. At 385 K the tabulated 6.832 mol/kg is greater than the hot concentrate salt/water ratio; no solids are assumed in EV-101.",
  "No crystal-size distribution, residence-time/nucleation prediction, crystal moisture or salt losses. Thermal duties include sensible and evaporation enthalpies; electrolyte excess/dissolution enthalpy is not modeled.",
  "Reference: https://doi.org/10.1515/pac-2021-1002 (IUPAC Technical Report, sodium chloride/water solubility Table 7)."
 ]
